[{:db/id 17592186124508 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b000b980-8b9a-5a4e-a59b-6de7017a3b28" "question-85da25d6-54a2-55b2-b4ae-23095c708e42"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fd86946f-a577-5d18-8f57-7b7435272376"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124318 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If ![](images/77/77c0dd8d9b925b3310c5470f272b59e2b9d25bb141295741f1748771b6c454c1.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\nII. If ![](images/86/86c4f440750b5d7bf45e8c36b6fd9852c2749ac56331b3e0d76a6901acaf5b60.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n\nIII. If ![](images/22/2295be7f70c3de36b51784b2919af95695f5520abdb2300287a17852b4cbfce3.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124510 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-83850766-9b1b-5a37-bf38-12d47d12c4d5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124319 :question/problem "Given ![](images/82/829e66e040815801f77e92b2afd97531779864935faf7c9dcf1b0485593db856.svg) what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-b000b980-8b9a-5a4e-a59b-6de7017a3b28" :question/id #uuid "b000b980-8b9a-5a4e-a59b-6de7017a3b28" :question/math-academy-id "q-34901" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $7\\times 11$ matrix that has $7$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A.$\n\nSince we are told that $A$ has $7$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-72b3a9a3-a8e1-52c0-99d6-ec57e4d43b0c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-72b3a9a3-a8e1-52c0-99d6-ec57e4d43b0c" :answer-field/id #uuid "72b3a9a3-a8e1-52c0-99d6-ec57e4d43b0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-53593f8a-84e1-5e46-9090-20482d8e60a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-942dbaf5-ecc1-59dd-96cd-09e8f4c50159" "answer-f87f31f4-b42f-5af1-a0e6-59a42452095b" "answer-1b7137d1-196e-5467-891f-8a544f21aeba" "answer-53593f8a-84e1-5e46-9090-20482d8e60a5" "answer-d1b97ca4-654d-53cf-b7f4-3b50efd771a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-942dbaf5-ecc1-59dd-96cd-09e8f4c50159" :answer/id #uuid "942dbaf5-ecc1-59dd-96cd-09e8f4c50159" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f87f31f4-b42f-5af1-a0e6-59a42452095b" :answer/id #uuid "f87f31f4-b42f-5af1-a0e6-59a42452095b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b7137d1-196e-5467-891f-8a544f21aeba" :answer/id #uuid "1b7137d1-196e-5467-891f-8a544f21aeba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53593f8a-84e1-5e46-9090-20482d8e60a5" :answer/id #uuid "53593f8a-84e1-5e46-9090-20482d8e60a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1b97ca4-654d-53cf-b7f4-3b50efd771a5" :answer/id #uuid "d1b97ca4-654d-53cf-b7f4-3b50efd771a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-85da25d6-54a2-55b2-b4ae-23095c708e42" :question/id #uuid "85da25d6-54a2-55b2-b4ae-23095c708e42" :question/math-academy-id "q-79338" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $4\\times 6$ matrix that has $4$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(B))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $B.$\n\nSince we are told that $B$ has $4$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f829e1c6-fc4a-5157-b1d9-91868b24b67e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f829e1c6-fc4a-5157-b1d9-91868b24b67e" :answer-field/id #uuid "f829e1c6-fc4a-5157-b1d9-91868b24b67e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3658fbf4-7125-51a3-8c67-6dac5efe7ee1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-51f6e2e6-dc2b-5315-9b73-948670576a5f" "answer-6da18174-0469-5de1-85a3-4a634932a54e" "answer-ce1d5e0a-36bb-506c-8445-a60981eb2cf5" "answer-3658fbf4-7125-51a3-8c67-6dac5efe7ee1" "answer-ef53b2d3-1206-58e8-a659-33784ef08b53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51f6e2e6-dc2b-5315-9b73-948670576a5f" :answer/id #uuid "51f6e2e6-dc2b-5315-9b73-948670576a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6da18174-0469-5de1-85a3-4a634932a54e" :answer/id #uuid "6da18174-0469-5de1-85a3-4a634932a54e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce1d5e0a-36bb-506c-8445-a60981eb2cf5" :answer/id #uuid "ce1d5e0a-36bb-506c-8445-a60981eb2cf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3658fbf4-7125-51a3-8c67-6dac5efe7ee1" :answer/id #uuid "3658fbf4-7125-51a3-8c67-6dac5efe7ee1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef53b2d3-1206-58e8-a659-33784ef08b53" :answer/id #uuid "ef53b2d3-1206-58e8-a659-33784ef08b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fd86946f-a577-5d18-8f57-7b7435272376" :question/id #uuid "fd86946f-a577-5d18-8f57-7b7435272376" :question/math-academy-id "q-35200" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0+1+2=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f7861d69-8891-56f9-b3bb-6cd69873e91d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f7861d69-8891-56f9-b3bb-6cd69873e91d" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7861d69-8891-56f9-b3bb-6cd69873e91d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-25d9c3ae-c60e-5f23-8b09-bd6f72672565" :answer-field/choices ["answer-62c579bb-353a-5222-8c49-b704acbe87e7" "answer-b08e9ade-c6e5-5b60-ac34-32e78a9a1641" "answer-8d34d79c-138f-5ab3-9fb5-c6f333384a8e" "answer-25d9c3ae-c60e-5f23-8b09-bd6f72672565" "answer-bca9b8c9-b194-53fd-be09-17e6ac4e9236"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62c579bb-353a-5222-8c49-b704acbe87e7" :answer/id #uuid "62c579bb-353a-5222-8c49-b704acbe87e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b08e9ade-c6e5-5b60-ac34-32e78a9a1641" :answer/id #uuid "b08e9ade-c6e5-5b60-ac34-32e78a9a1641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d34d79c-138f-5ab3-9fb5-c6f333384a8e" :answer/id #uuid "8d34d79c-138f-5ab3-9fb5-c6f333384a8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25d9c3ae-c60e-5f23-8b09-bd6f72672565" :answer/id #uuid "25d9c3ae-c60e-5f23-8b09-bd6f72672565" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bca9b8c9-b194-53fd-be09-17e6ac4e9236" :answer/id #uuid "bca9b8c9-b194-53fd-be09-17e6ac4e9236" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186319352 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n\nII. If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$\n\nIII. If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-83850766-9b1b-5a37-bf38-12d47d12c4d5" :question/id #uuid "83850766-9b1b-5a37-bf38-12d47d12c4d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-35347" :question/problem "Given $G=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))$, we reduce $G$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{11}{4} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c9771c3-f30b-56b9-83e9-dd0e274a3d9d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c9771c3-f30b-56b9-83e9-dd0e274a3d9d" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9771c3-f30b-56b9-83e9-dd0e274a3d9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-48411ad1-c867-5f45-b8c7-ce3589fd2218" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48411ad1-c867-5f45-b8c7-ce3589fd2218" "answer-01b39024-8f98-5edf-93f7-04a64ee7b6c0" "answer-d56c921a-e74a-5b91-bee7-d13092469fb1" "answer-7ac52ed7-ea31-518a-95fb-dc6ea725ad9d" "answer-69951a24-a52b-5841-8392-9e70e2c63d9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48411ad1-c867-5f45-b8c7-ce3589fd2218" :answer/id #uuid "48411ad1-c867-5f45-b8c7-ce3589fd2218" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01b39024-8f98-5edf-93f7-04a64ee7b6c0" :answer/id #uuid "01b39024-8f98-5edf-93f7-04a64ee7b6c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d56c921a-e74a-5b91-bee7-d13092469fb1" :answer/id #uuid "d56c921a-e74a-5b91-bee7-d13092469fb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ac52ed7-ea31-518a-95fb-dc6ea725ad9d" :answer/id #uuid "7ac52ed7-ea31-518a-95fb-dc6ea725ad9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69951a24-a52b-5841-8392-9e70e2c63d9d" :answer/id #uuid "69951a24-a52b-5841-8392-9e70e2c63d9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125778 :tutorial/content "We already learned that the rank of a matrix $A$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ Now, can we obtain any information from the *non-pivot* columns?\n\nThe answer is yes! The non-pivot columns help to find the dimension of the null space of a matrix $A,$ and here's how.\n\nConsider the matrix \n![](images/99/991b6f0c69e6341620139db9bfce5303785be21760eb8d630bfee92c57d4bc6a.svg)\n\nThe matrix $A$ is already in row echelon form, where the $1$st and the $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd one is a *non-pivot* column. Now, to get the null space of $A,$ we need to find the solution of the system\n\n![](images/1c/1cd56dc26ad4f478c3d7cb14375b8b2e45ef68e3215e79494d56108fecec39cb.svg)\n\nwhere $\\color{blue}x_1$ and ${\\color{blue}x_3}$ are basic variables and $\\color{red}x_2$ is a free variable. Hence, we obtain that \n\n![](images/56/56587dc5c1c98493060edb3561c13aa1576187461418619684459dd1f55626fe.svg)\n\nis a basis of $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))={\\color{red}1}$.\n\nIn other words,\n\n$\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is equal to the number of *non-pivot* columns in the corresponding row echelon form of $A$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$  is the number of *free variables* in the corresponding homogeneous system with the coefficient matrix $A.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124684 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
